Keep the weak references to an object in the runtime, not the object.

Every JSObject had a first_weak_ref pointer, and on Reddit's home page
1.4% of objects had a weak reference (a WeakMap or WeakSet key, a
WeakRef or FinalizationRegistry target). The runtime now keeps a hash
table from object to its list (rt->weak_obj_hash, JSWeakObjNode), and
the object has one bit, has_weak_ref. weak_obj_prepare makes an
object's node before anything else is set up for a new weak reference,
so insert_weakref_record cannot fail; the node goes when the object is
freed (weak_obj_reset). Symbols used as weak keys keep their pointer
in the atom.

JSObject falls from 72 to 64 bytes on 64-bit hosts and from 36 to 32
on 32-bit ones; with the allocator's 8-byte block header an object
moves from the 80-byte to the 72-byte class on the host and from the
48-byte to the 40-byte class on the PowerPC. Reddit's 230,000 objects
take about 1.8 MB less.

